{
	"liturgiFormat": 1,
	"kind": "template",
	"data": {
		"id": "ordning-for-hovedgudstjenesten-engelsk",
		"name": "Ordning for hovedgudstjenesten (Engelsk)",
		"malForm": "Engelsk",
		"liturgiType": "gudstjeneste",
		"kanGudstjeneste": true,
		"sections": [
			{
				"title": "Uten tittel",
				"items": [
					{
						"id": "i-mwrtxqzr-0",
						"type": "tekst",
						"heading": "The order of the",
						"instr": "",
						"text": "",
						"alts": [],
						"selAlt": 0,
						"enabled": true,
						"optional": false,
						"salmeNr": "",
						"salmeTittel": ""
					},
					{
						"id": "i-mwrtxqzs-1",
						"type": "tekst",
						"heading": "Principal serviceAuthorised by General Synod in 2019",
						"instr": "",
						"text": "The letter C stands for congregation, the letter A stands for all service participants (priest/liturgist and congregation), and the letter L stands for liturgist (service leaders, priest, or another person who has a bishops’ permission to administer the service). CL (co-liturgist) is used to indicate roles for readers, prayer leaders, communion assistants, cantors, choirs and others who perform liturgical tasks. When there are two letters, L/CL or CL/L, the first has primacy. More elaborate descriptions of the tasks of the liturgist and the co-liturgists may be found in the guidelines on different parts of the service in the Service handbook.",
						"alts": [],
						"selAlt": 0,
						"enabled": true,
						"optional": false,
						"salmeNr": "",
						"salmeTittel": ""
					},
					{
						"id": "i-mwrtxqzs-2",
						"type": "tekst",
						"heading": "The Gathering",
						"instr": "@NOTAT Bell ringing\n@NOTAT Brief information about the service of the day presented by a co-liturgist or liturgist.",
						"text": "1 Preparation\nThe church may be open before the service starts, for the congregation to light candles, sit in silence, reflection and prayer.\nHere or after section 3 Greeting, may follow:\nThis information concludes with: CL/L | Let us be still before God. Short silence, a bell is then rung three times.\nAn asterisk (*) marks sections when it is customary for the congregation to stand.",
						"alts": [],
						"selAlt": 0,
						"enabled": true,
						"optional": false,
						"salmeNr": "",
						"salmeTittel": ""
					},
					{
						"id": "i-mwrtxqzs-3",
						"type": "tekst",
						"heading": "* 2 Entrance hymn",
						"instr": "",
						"text": "{{r}}A |{{/r}} prelude may be performed. This is normally in the character of a chorale prelude to the entrance hymn.\nThere may be a procession during the prelude/introduction and/or the entrance hymn. The procession cross is carried first in the procession. A candle, the Bible, baptism water, bread and wine may also be presented.\nIf bread and wine have not already been placed on a credence table, or on the altar before the service, they are carried in the procession and then placed on the credence table or on the altar.\nThe congregation stands during the procession, Entrance hymn and Greeting.",
						"alts": [],
						"selAlt": 0,
						"enabled": true,
						"optional": false,
						"salmeNr": "",
						"salmeTittel": ""
					},
					{
						"id": "i-mwrtxqzs-4",
						"type": "tekst",
						"heading": "* 3 Greeting",
						"instr": "",
						"text": "When there is a baptism within the principal service, one of the two first greetings may be chosen.\nBefore the first two greetings, the liturgist may say: Dear congregation:\n{{r}}L |{{/r}} Grace be with you and peace\nfrom God, our Father, and the Lord Jesus Christ.",
						"alts": [],
						"selAlt": 0,
						"enabled": true,
						"optional": false,
						"salmeNr": "",
						"salmeTittel": ""
					},
					{
						"id": "i-mwrtxqzs-5",
						"type": "tekst",
						"heading": "or",
						"instr": "",
						"text": "{{r}}L |{{/r}} The grace of our Lord Jesus Christ, the love of God\nand the communion of the Holy Spirit be with you all.",
						"alts": [],
						"selAlt": 0,
						"enabled": true,
						"optional": false,
						"salmeNr": "",
						"salmeTittel": ""
					},
					{
						"id": "i-mwrtxqzs-6",
						"type": "tekst",
						"heading": "or",
						"instr": "",
						"text": "{{r}}L |{{/r}} In the name of the Father and of the Son and of the Holy Spirit .",
						"alts": [],
						"selAlt": 0,
						"enabled": true,
						"optional": false,
						"salmeNr": "",
						"salmeTittel": ""
					},
					{
						"id": "i-mwrtxqzs-7",
						"type": "tekst",
						"heading": "or",
						"instr": "",
						"text": "{{r}}L |{{/r}} In the name of the Father and of the Son and of the Holy Spirit : Our creator, redeemer and sanctifier.\nThe congregation is seated.\nIf a brief introduction to the service has not been given during section 1, it may be given here.\n4 Gathering prayer\nSee Gathering prayers and their use.\n{{r}}CL |{{/r}} Let us pray.\nBIBELREF | either 1\n{{r}}CL |{{/r}} God, we have entered into your holy house to receive your gifts. Open our hearts, so that we may be renewed in our faith in you.\nBIBELREF | or 2\n{{r}}CL |{{/r}} Holy God, we are gathered in your presence to receive your love and truth. Send us your Spirit, and open us to your gifts. Let your word take root in our hearts, so that Christ may live in us, and we become one in you to serve you in all things.\nBIBELREF | or 3\n{{r}}CL |{{/r}} Gracious God, you give life to all that lives, we thank you for the beauty of the earth,\nand for everything that shows us your greatness. Here, in your presence, we pray: Give us listening ears, thankful hearts, and serving hands, so that we may hear your word, praise you for your goodness, and in word and deed bear witness to your splendours.\n{{r}}CL |{{/r}} God, we pray.\n{{r}}A |{{/r}} Amen.\n5 The confession\nFollows here or as section 17.\nThe confession begins with:\n{{r}}L |{{/r}} Let us bow before God and confess our sins.",
						"alts": [],
						"selAlt": 0,
						"enabled": true,
						"optional": false,
						"salmeNr": "",
						"salmeTittel": ""
					},
					{
						"id": "i-mwrtxqzs-8",
						"type": "tekst",
						"heading": "or",
						"instr": "",
						"text": "{{r}}L |{{/r}} Let us bow before God and pray for forgiveness.",
						"alts": [],
						"selAlt": 0,
						"enabled": true,
						"optional": false,
						"salmeNr": "",
						"salmeTittel": ""
					},
					{
						"id": "i-mwrtxqzs-9",
						"type": "tekst",
						"heading": "or",
						"instr": "",
						"text": "{{r}}L |{{/r}} Trusting in God’s grace, let us confess our sins.",
						"alts": [],
						"selAlt": 0,
						"enabled": true,
						"optional": false,
						"salmeNr": "",
						"salmeTittel": ""
					},
					{
						"id": "i-mwrtxqzs-10",
						"type": "tekst",
						"heading": "or",
						"instr": "@NOTAT Short silence",
						"text": "{{r}}L |{{/r}} Trusting in God’s grace, let us pray for forgiveness.\nThe priest kneels during the confession and silence. The congregation may also kneel.",
						"alts": [],
						"selAlt": 0,
						"enabled": true,
						"optional": false,
						"salmeNr": "",
						"salmeTittel": ""
					},
					{
						"id": "i-mwrtxqzs-11",
						"type": "tekst",
						"heading": "either a",
						"instr": "",
						"text": "{{r}}A |{{/r}} God, have mercy on me!",
						"alts": [],
						"selAlt": 0,
						"enabled": true,
						"optional": false,
						"salmeNr": "",
						"salmeTittel": ""
					},
					{
						"id": "i-mwrtxqzs-12",
						"type": "tekst",
						"heading": "I have sinned against you and betrayed my neighbour",
						"instr": "",
						"text": "– in thoughts and words, in what I have done and in what I have left undone.\nForgive my sins for the sake of Jesus Christ. Create in me a clean heart,\nand strengthen me in a new life with your Holy Spirit.",
						"alts": [],
						"selAlt": 0,
						"enabled": true,
						"optional": false,
						"salmeNr": "",
						"salmeTittel": ""
					},
					{
						"id": "i-mwrtxqzs-13",
						"type": "tekst",
						"heading": "or b",
						"instr": "",
						"text": "{{r}}A |{{/r}} God, have mercy on me!\nForgive my sins for the sake of Jesus Christ. Create in me a clean heart,\nand strengthen me in a new life with your Holy Spirit.",
						"alts": [],
						"selAlt": 0,
						"enabled": true,
						"optional": false,
						"salmeNr": "",
						"salmeTittel": ""
					},
					{
						"id": "i-mwrtxqzs-14",
						"type": "tekst",
						"heading": "or c",
						"instr": "",
						"text": "{{r}}A |{{/r}} God, you know and love us all. You want us to care for each other and the world.\nWe know that we have failed and acted against you. Forgive us and help us, for the sake of Jesus.",
						"alts": [],
						"selAlt": 0,
						"enabled": true,
						"optional": false,
						"salmeNr": "",
						"salmeTittel": ""
					},
					{
						"id": "i-mwrtxqzs-15",
						"type": "tekst",
						"heading": "or d",
						"instr": "@NOTAT The music and words of the parts of the ordinary of the mass are normally taken from the Church of Norway’s five authorised ordinary settings. See the music in Liturgisk musikk (2020) or Gudstjenestebok for Den norske kirke (2020).",
						"text": "{{r}}A |{{/r}} Holy God, our creator, have mercy on us.\nWe have sinned against you and broken your commandments.\nForgive us for the sake of Jesus. Set us free so that we may serve you, care for your creation, and meet our neighbour with love.\nThe confession in the Order from 1977 may also be used:\nHoly God, heavenly Father. Look with grace on me, a sinful person, who has acted against you in thought, word and deed, and who harbours evil inclinations in my heart.\nFor the sake of Jesus Christ, have patience with me.\nForgive all my sins and allow me to revere and love you alone.\nIn certain services, other confessions than these five alternatives may be used. The prayer may be taken from a variety of sources, or formulated locally.\nFollowing the confession, the liturgist may give an absolution:\n{{r}}L |{{/r}} The Word of God says, “If we confess our sins, he who is faithful and just will forgive us our sins and cleanse us from all unrighteousness.”\n1 John 1:9\nor\n{{r}}L |{{/r}} “For as the heavens are high above the earth, so great is his steadfast love towards those who fear him; as far as the east is from the west, so far he removes our transgressions from us.”\nPsalm 103:11-12\n6 KYRIE and 7 Song of praise GLORIA\nThe Kyrie and Gloria are normally sung.\nThe Gloria may be omitted in Lent.\nBIBELREF | Series 1",
						"alts": [],
						"selAlt": 0,
						"enabled": true,
						"optional": false,
						"salmeNr": "",
						"salmeTittel": ""
					},
					{
						"id": "i-mwrtxqzs-16",
						"type": "tekst",
						"heading": "either",
						"instr": "",
						"text": "BIBELREF | Kyrie 1a\n{{r}}A |{{/r}} Kyrie eleison. God our Father, have mercy on us.\nChriste eleison. Lord Christ, have mercy on us.\nKyrie eleison. Holy Spirit, have mercy on us.",
						"alts": [],
						"selAlt": 0,
						"enabled": true,
						"optional": false,
						"salmeNr": "",
						"salmeTittel": ""
					},
					{
						"id": "i-mwrtxqzt-17",
						"type": "tekst",
						"heading": "or",
						"instr": "",
						"text": "BIBELREF | Kyrie 1b",
						"alts": [],
						"selAlt": 0,
						"enabled": true,
						"optional": false,
						"salmeNr": "",
						"salmeTittel": ""
					},
					{
						"id": "i-mwrtxqzt-18",
						"type": "tekst",
						"heading": "See N13: 976.6 with words in Bokmål and Sami",
						"instr": "",
						"text": "",
						"alts": [],
						"selAlt": 0,
						"enabled": true,
						"optional": false,
						"salmeNr": "",
						"salmeTittel": ""
					},
					{
						"id": "i-mwrtxqzt-19",
						"type": "tekst",
						"heading": "Northern-Sami",
						"instr": "",
						"text": "{{r}}A |{{/r}} Kyrie eleison. Ipmil Áhččámet árpmit min.\nChriste eleison. Hearrámet Kristus árpmit min.\nKyrie eleison. Bassi Vuoigŋa árpmit min.",
						"alts": [],
						"selAlt": 0,
						"enabled": true,
						"optional": false,
						"salmeNr": "",
						"salmeTittel": ""
					},
					{
						"id": "i-mwrtxqzt-20",
						"type": "tekst",
						"heading": "either",
						"instr": "",
						"text": "BIBELREF | Gloria 1a\n{{r}}L/CL |{{/r}} Glory to God in the highest\n{{r}}A |{{/r}} and peace to his people on earth.\nWe worship you, we give you thanks, we praise you for your glory.\nWhen the short version is used: Amen.\nWhen the full version (Laudamus) is used:\n{{r}}CL |{{/r}} We praise you and the splendours of your works, Lord God, heavenly king, almighty Father.\n{{r}}A |{{/r}} We worship you, we give you thanks, we praise you for your glory.\n{{r}}CL |{{/r}} Lord Jesus Christ, only Son of the Father, Lord God, Lamb of God, you take away the sin of the world: have mercy on us; you are seated at the right hand of the Father: hear our prayer.\n{{r}}A |{{/r}} We worship you, we give you thanks, we praise you for your glory.\n{{r}}CL |{{/r}} For you alone are Holy, you alone are the Lord, you alone are the most high, Jesus Christ, with the Holy Spirit, in the glory of God the Father.\n{{r}}A |{{/r}} We worship you, we give you thanks, we praise you for your glory. Amen\nor Gloria 1b (for music score, see N13: 276 Alene Gud i himmerik)\n{{r}}A |{{/r}} All glory be to God on high,\nand peace on earth from heaven,\nand God’s good will unfailingly\nbe to all people given.\nWe bless, we worship you,\nwe raise for your great glory\nthanks and praise,\n{{r}}O |{{/r}} God, almighty Father.\n{{r}}O |{{/r}} Lamb of God, Lord Jesus Christ,\nwhom God the Father gave us,\nwho for the world was sacrificed\nup on the cross to save us;\nand, as you sit at God’s right hand\nand we for judgement\nthere must stand,\nhave mercy, Lord, upon us.\nYou only are the Holy One,\nwho came for our salvation,\nand only you are God’s true Son,\nwho was before creation.\nYou, only, Christ, as Lord we own,\nand with the Spirit, you alone\nshare in the Father’s glory.",
						"alts": [],
						"selAlt": 0,
						"enabled": true,
						"optional": false,
						"salmeNr": "",
						"salmeTittel": ""
					},
					{
						"id": "i-mwrtxqzt-21",
						"type": "tekst",
						"heading": "or",
						"instr": "",
						"text": "BIBELREF | Gloria 1c\nThe hymn ‘Måne og sol’ (N13: 240), with the following or another introduction:\n{{r}}L/CL |{{/r}} Sing for the Lord, praise his name. Speak of his salvation every day.",
						"alts": [],
						"selAlt": 0,
						"enabled": true,
						"optional": false,
						"salmeNr": "",
						"salmeTittel": ""
					},
					{
						"id": "i-mwrtxqzt-22",
						"type": "tekst",
						"heading": "or",
						"instr": "",
						"text": "\nBIBELREF | Series 2\n{{r}}A |{{/r}} Kyrie eleison, have mercy on us.\nChriste eleison, have mercy on us.\nKyrie eleison, have mercy on us.\n{{r}}L/CL |{{/r}} Glory to God in the highest\n{{r}}A |{{/r}} and peace to his people on earth.\nWe worship you, we give you thanks, we praise you for your glory.\nWhen the short version is used: Amen.\nWhen the full version (Laudamus) is used:\n{{r}}CL |{{/r}} Praise be to God, our creator, we celebrate your creation.\n{{r}}A |{{/r}} We worship you, we give you thanks, we praise you for your glory.\n{{r}}CL |{{/r}} Praise be to Jesus, our saviour, you show us the way to life.\n{{r}}A |{{/r}} We worship you, we give you thanks, we praise you for your glory.\n{{r}}CL |{{/r}} Praise be to the Spirit, our comforter, you fill us with joy and peace.",
						"alts": [],
						"selAlt": 0,
						"enabled": true,
						"optional": false,
						"salmeNr": "",
						"salmeTittel": ""
					},
					{
						"id": "i-mwrtxqzt-23",
						"type": "tekst",
						"heading": "or",
						"instr": "",
						"text": "\nBIBELREF | Series 3\n{{r}}CL |{{/r}} Lord, have mercy on us.\n{{r}}C |{{/r}} Lord, have mercy on us.\n{{r}}CL |{{/r}} Christ, have mercy on us.\n{{r}}C |{{/r}} Christ, have mercy on us.\n{{r}}CL |{{/r}} Lord, have mercy on us.\n{{r}}C |{{/r}} Lord, have mercy on us.\n{{r}}L/CL |{{/r}} Glory to God in the highest.\n{{r}}A |{{/r}} Glory to God in the highest.\n{{r}}CL |{{/r}} We worship you, Lord. We praise you, Lord.\n{{r}}A |{{/r}} Glory to God in the highest.\nWhen the short version is used: Amen.\nWhen the full version (Laudamus) is used:\n{{r}}CL |{{/r}} Lord, we thank you for your greatness.\n{{r}}A |{{/r}} Glory to God in the highest.\n{{r}}CL |{{/r}} Lord God, Our Father, you are almighty\n{{r}}A |{{/r}} Glory to God in the highest.\n{{r}}CL |{{/r}} Lord Jesus Christ, you are God’s only son.\n{{r}}A |{{/r}} Glory to God in the highest.\n{{r}}CL |{{/r}} Lord, you are holy, you are merciful.\n{{r}}A |{{/r}} Glory to God in the highest.\n{{r}}CL |{{/r}} You are the most high, Lord Jesus Christ.\n{{r}}A |{{/r}} Glory to God in the highest. Amen.",
						"alts": [],
						"selAlt": 0,
						"enabled": true,
						"optional": false,
						"salmeNr": "",
						"salmeTittel": ""
					},
					{
						"id": "i-mwrtxqzt-24",
						"type": "tekst",
						"heading": "or",
						"instr": "",
						"text": "",
						"alts": [],
						"selAlt": 0,
						"enabled": true,
						"optional": false,
						"salmeNr": "",
						"salmeTittel": ""
					},
					{
						"id": "i-mwrtxqzt-25",
						"type": "tekst",
						"heading": "Series for festivals (Christmas, Easter and Pentecost)",
						"instr": "",
						"text": "{{r}}CL |{{/r}} Kyrie eleison.\n{{r}}A |{{/r}} Kyrie eleison.\n{{r}}CL |{{/r}} Christe eleison.\n{{r}}A |{{/r}} Christe eleison.\n{{r}}CL |{{/r}} Kyrie eleison.\n{{r}}A |{{/r}} Kyrie eleison.\n{{r}}L/CL |{{/r}} Glory to God in the highest\n{{r}}A |{{/r}} and peace to his people on earth.\nWe worship you, we give you thanks, we praise you for your glory.\nWhen the short version is used: Amen.\nWhen the full version (Laudamus) is used:\n{{r}}CL |{{/r}} We praise you for your greatness, Lord God, heavenly king, almighty Father.\n{{r}}C |{{/r}} We worship you, we give you thanks, we praise you for your glory.\n{{r}}CL |{{/r}} Lord, only Son of the Father, Jesus Christ, Lamb of God, you take away the sin of the world: have mercy on us. You are seated at the right hand of the Father, receive our prayer.\n{{r}}C |{{/r}} We worship you, we give you thanks, we praise you for your glory.\n{{r}}CL |{{/r}} For you alone are Holy, you alone are the Lord, you alone are the most high, Jesus Christ, with the Holy Spirit, in the glory of God the Father.\n{{r}}C |{{/r}} We worship you, we give you thanks, we praise you for your glory. Amen.",
						"alts": [],
						"selAlt": 0,
						"enabled": true,
						"optional": false,
						"salmeNr": "",
						"salmeTittel": ""
					},
					{
						"id": "i-mwrtxqzt-26",
						"type": "tekst",
						"heading": "or",
						"instr": "",
						"text": "",
						"alts": [],
						"selAlt": 0,
						"enabled": true,
						"optional": false,
						"salmeNr": "",
						"salmeTittel": ""
					},
					{
						"id": "i-mwrtxqzt-27",
						"type": "tekst",
						"heading": "Series for Lent",
						"instr": "@NOTAT Baptisms in the principal service normally take place here.\n@NOTAT See Prayer of the Day.",
						"text": "{{r}}C |{{/r}} Kyrie eleison. Lord, have mercy on us.\nChriste eleison. Christ, have mercy on us.\nKyrie eleison. Lord, have mercy on us.\nIn the series for Lent, no setting of the Gloria is provided.\nFor certain occasions the prayer can be expressed as a litany (N13: 981) or as a locally formed Kyrie litany with recessions from N13: 976. For other specific services another Kyrie may also be used.\nFor certain services another Gloria or one or more Gloria recessions may be used.\n8 Prayer of the day (Collect)\nThe prayer of the day may be omitted. The prayer is sung or recited.\nThe prayer begins with:\n{{r}}L |{{/r}} Let us pray.\nThe prayer ends with:\n{{r}}C |{{/r}} Amen.",
						"alts": [],
						"selAlt": 0,
						"enabled": true,
						"optional": false,
						"salmeNr": "",
						"salmeTittel": ""
					},
					{
						"id": "i-mwrtxqzt-28",
						"type": "tekst",
						"heading": "The Word",
						"instr": "",
						"text": "In other Principal Services than the High Mass, there may be two readings, or one reading (the Gospel). If so, section 10 Psalm/Hymn may be omitted. The congregation stands during the Gospel reading and sits during the other readings.\n{{r}}L/CL |{{/r}} Let us hear the word of the Lord.\n9 First reading\nFrom the Old Testament\n{{r}}CL |{{/r}} The first reading is from …\nThe reading ends with:\n{{r}}CL |{{/r}} This is the word of the Lord.\n10 Psalm / Hymn\n{{r}}A |{{/r}} psalm or appropriate hymn may be sung, or there may be a short silence between the readings.\n11 Second reading\nFrom the New Testament excluding the Gospels\n{{r}}CL |{{/r}} The second reading is from …\nThe reading ends with:\n{{r}}CL |{{/r}} This is the word of the Lord.",
						"alts": [],
						"selAlt": 0,
						"enabled": true,
						"optional": false,
						"salmeNr": "",
						"salmeTittel": ""
					},
					{
						"id": "i-mwrtxqzt-29",
						"type": "tekst",
						"heading": "* 12 The Gospel",
						"instr": "@NOTAT Alleluia\n@NOTAT Gospel reading\n@NOTAT Response",
						"text": "The Gospel reading may begin with an alleluia response with or without a suitable verse, or a short hymn.\n{{r}}A |{{/r}} gospel procession may be integrated. The person carrying the Bible may be joined by people carrying candles.\nSee “Alleluia response” in N13: 977.1-7.\nDuring Lent, Alleluia may be replaced with a choral response suitable for the season. These hymns may be sung as a tract: N13: 926, 927, 928, 932 og 939.\n{{r}}L/CL |{{/r}} Hear the Gospel of our Lord Jesus Christ according to …\nThe reading ends with:\n{{r}}L/CL |{{/r}} This is the Gospel of the Lord.\nThe congregation or choir may respond with an Alleluia response, or with a short hymn or another appropriate response. On first days a festival verse may be sung as a response (13: 41, 193, 228).\n13 The sermon\nThe preacher preaches on the gospel text or another sermon text.\nThe sermon may end with one of the following doxologies:\n{{r}}L |{{/r}} Glory be to the Father and to the Son and to the Holy Spirit, \nas it was in the beginning, is now and ever shall be. Amen.",
						"alts": [],
						"selAlt": 0,
						"enabled": true,
						"optional": false,
						"salmeNr": "",
						"salmeTittel": ""
					},
					{
						"id": "i-mwrtxqzt-30",
						"type": "tekst",
						"heading": "or",
						"instr": "",
						"text": "{{r}}L |{{/r}} Glory be to the Father and to the Son and to the Holy Spirit : Our creator, redeemer and sanctifier.\nAfter the sermon, a moment of silence may be held, or a short hymn may be sung. Alternatively, meditative music may be performed.",
						"alts": [],
						"selAlt": 0,
						"enabled": true,
						"optional": false,
						"salmeNr": "",
						"salmeTittel": ""
					},
					{
						"id": "i-mwrtxqzt-31",
						"type": "tekst",
						"heading": "* 14 The creed – The confession of faith",
						"instr": "",
						"text": "The creed may be sung or said.\nWhen baptisms are included in the Principal Service, the creed may be omitted at this point. Alternatively, a creedal hymn may be sung.\n{{r}}CL/L |{{/r}} Let us confess our holy faith.\n{{r}}A |{{/r}} I believe in God, the Father almighty,\ncreator of heaven and earth.\nI believe in Jesus Christ, his only Son, our Lord,\nwho was conceived by the Holy Spirit,\nborn of the Virgin Mary,\nsuffered under Pontius Pilate,\nwas crucified, died, and was buried;\nhe descended to the dead.\nOn the third day he rose again;\nhe ascended into heaven,\nhe is seated at the right hand of the Father,\nand he will come to judge the living and the dead.\nI believe in the Holy Spirit,\nthe holy catholic Church,\nthe communion of saints,\nthe forgiveness of sins,\nthe resurrection of the body,\nand the life everlasting.",
						"alts": [],
						"selAlt": 0,
						"enabled": true,
						"optional": false,
						"salmeNr": "",
						"salmeTittel": ""
					},
					{
						"id": "i-mwrtxqzt-32",
						"type": "tekst",
						"heading": "Amen . The Apostle’s Creed",
						"instr": "",
						"text": "",
						"alts": [],
						"selAlt": 0,
						"enabled": true,
						"optional": false,
						"salmeNr": "",
						"salmeTittel": ""
					},
					{
						"id": "i-mwrtxqzt-33",
						"type": "tekst",
						"heading": "or",
						"instr": "",
						"text": "{{r}}A |{{/r}} We believe in one God,\nthe Father, the Almighty,\nmaker of heaven and earth,\nof all that is, seen and unseen.\nWe believe in one Lord, Jesus Christ,\nthe only Son of God,\neternally begotten of the Father,\nGod from God, Light from Light,\ntrue God from true God,\nbegotten, not made,\nof one Being with the Father;\nthrough him all things were made.\nFor us men and for our salvation he came down from heaven,\nwas incarnate from the Holy Spirit and the Virgin Mary\nand was made man.\nFor our sake he was crucified under Pontius Pilate;\nhe suffered death and was buried.",
						"alts": [],
						"selAlt": 0,
						"enabled": true,
						"optional": false,
						"salmeNr": "",
						"salmeTittel": ""
					},
					{
						"id": "i-mwrtxqzt-34",
						"type": "tekst",
						"heading": "On the third day he rose again",
						"instr": "",
						"text": "in accordance with the scriptures;\nhe ascended into heaven\nand is seated at the right hand of the Father.\nHe will come again in glory to judge the living and the dead,\nand his kingdom will have no end.\nWe believe in the Holy Spirit,\nthe Lord, the giver of life,\nwho proceeds from the Father and the Son,\nwho with the Father and the Son is worshipped and glorified,\nwho has spoken through the prophets.\nWe believe in one holy catholic and apostolic Church.\nWe acknowledge one baptism for the forgiveness of sins.\nWe look for the resurrection of the dead,\nand the life of the world to come.\nAmen. The Nicene Creed.\n15 Hymn\nThe hymn may be omitted if the creed is sung. The hymn may alternatively be sung between section 13 Sermon and section 14 The Creed.\n16 Notices\nThe notices may be announced here or at another suitable point in the service, or shared with the congregation in another manner.\n17 The confession\nMay be placed here or as a part of section 5.\nBefore the introductory words the liturgist may say:\n{{r}}L |{{/r}} Our Lord Jesus Christ said, “You shall love the Lord your God with all your heart, and with all your soul, and with all your mind.” This is the greatest and first commandment. But the second is equally great: “You shall love your neighbour as yourself.” Matthew 22:37-39\nThe confession ends with:\n{{r}}L |{{/r}} Let us bow before God and confess our sins.",
						"alts": [],
						"selAlt": 0,
						"enabled": true,
						"optional": false,
						"salmeNr": "",
						"salmeTittel": ""
					},
					{
						"id": "i-mwrtxqzt-35",
						"type": "tekst",
						"heading": "or",
						"instr": "",
						"text": "{{r}}L |{{/r}} Let us bow before God and pray for forgiveness.",
						"alts": [],
						"selAlt": 0,
						"enabled": true,
						"optional": false,
						"salmeNr": "",
						"salmeTittel": ""
					},
					{
						"id": "i-mwrtxqzt-36",
						"type": "tekst",
						"heading": "or",
						"instr": "",
						"text": "{{r}}L |{{/r}} Trusting in God’s grace, let us confess our sins.",
						"alts": [],
						"selAlt": 0,
						"enabled": true,
						"optional": false,
						"salmeNr": "",
						"salmeTittel": ""
					},
					{
						"id": "i-mwrtxqzt-37",
						"type": "tekst",
						"heading": "or",
						"instr": "@NOTAT Short silence",
						"text": "{{r}}L |{{/r}} Trusting in God’s grace, let us pray for forgiveness.\nThe priest kneels during the confession. Where possible, the congregation may also kneel.",
						"alts": [],
						"selAlt": 0,
						"enabled": true,
						"optional": false,
						"salmeNr": "",
						"salmeTittel": ""
					},
					{
						"id": "i-mwrtxqzt-38",
						"type": "tekst",
						"heading": "either a",
						"instr": "",
						"text": "{{r}}A |{{/r}} God, have mercy on me!",
						"alts": [],
						"selAlt": 0,
						"enabled": true,
						"optional": false,
						"salmeNr": "",
						"salmeTittel": ""
					},
					{
						"id": "i-mwrtxqzt-39",
						"type": "tekst",
						"heading": "I have sinned against you and betrayed my neighbour",
						"instr": "",
						"text": "– in thoughts and words, in what I have done and in what I have left undone.\nForgive my sins for the sake of Jesus Christ. Create in me a clean heart,\nand strengthen me in a new life with your Holy Spirit.",
						"alts": [],
						"selAlt": 0,
						"enabled": true,
						"optional": false,
						"salmeNr": "",
						"salmeTittel": ""
					},
					{
						"id": "i-mwrtxqzt-40",
						"type": "tekst",
						"heading": "or b",
						"instr": "",
						"text": "{{r}}A |{{/r}} God, have mercy on me!\nForgive my sins for the sake of Jesus Christ. Create in me a clean heart,\nand strengthen me in a new life with your Holy Spirit.",
						"alts": [],
						"selAlt": 0,
						"enabled": true,
						"optional": false,
						"salmeNr": "",
						"salmeTittel": ""
					},
					{
						"id": "i-mwrtxqzt-41",
						"type": "tekst",
						"heading": "or c",
						"instr": "",
						"text": "{{r}}A |{{/r}} God, you know and love us all. You want us to take care of each other and of the world.\nWe know that we have failed and acted against you. Forgive us and help us, for the sake of Jesus.",
						"alts": [],
						"selAlt": 0,
						"enabled": true,
						"optional": false,
						"salmeNr": "",
						"salmeTittel": ""
					},
					{
						"id": "i-mwrtxqzt-42",
						"type": "tekst",
						"heading": "or d",
						"instr": "@NOTAT See themes and models for the intercessions, and formulated intercessions and litanies.",
						"text": "{{r}}A |{{/r}} Holy God, our creator, have mercy on us.\nWe have sinned against you and broken your commandments.\nForgive us for the sake of Jesus. Set us free so that we may serve you,\ncare for your creation, and meet our neighbour with love.\nThe confession in the Order from 1977 may also be used:\nHoly God, heavenly Father, look with grace on me, a sinful person, who has acted against you in thought, word and deed, and who harbours evil inclinations in my heart.\nFor the sake of Jesus Christ, have patience with me.\nForgive all my sins and allow me to revere and love you alone.\nFor special services other confessions than these five alternatives may be used. The prayer can be taken from a variety of sources or formulated locally.\nFollowing the confession, the liturgist may give an absolution:\n{{r}}L |{{/r}} The Word of God says, “If we confess our sins, he who is faithful and just will forgive us our sins and cleanse us from all unrighteousness.” 1 John 1:9\nor\n{{r}}L |{{/r}} For as the heavens are high above the earth, so great is his steadfast love towards those who fear him; as far as the east is from the west, so far he removes our transgressions from us. Psalm 103: 11-12\n18 Intercessions for the church and the world\nThe intercessions may be formulated locally, or set prayers may be used. The intercessions are preferably led by a co-liturgist. The individual petitions may be read by several people.\nEach petition may end with:\n{{r}}CL/L |{{/r}} God, we pray.",
						"alts": [],
						"selAlt": 0,
						"enabled": true,
						"optional": false,
						"salmeNr": "",
						"salmeTittel": ""
					},
					{
						"id": "i-mwrtxqzt-43",
						"type": "tekst",
						"heading": "or",
						"instr": "@NOTAT Congregational response",
						"text": "{{r}}CL/L |{{/r}} God, hear our prayer.\nRead or sung by the petition leader.\nLocally formulated intercessions may be used related to the following themes:\n1 The peoples and nations of the world.\n2 Our own country and its people.\n3 The world-wide church and the church in our own country.\n4 Our congregation, families, and the place where we live.\n5 Current events.\n{{r}}A |{{/r}} prayer relating to current events may be placed in the category in which it most closely relates (1-4), or as a special petition (5). When the Principal Service includes (a) baptism(s) one of the three intercessions in the baptism liturgy (section 7), is prayed during the intercessions.\nDuring Lent and on the Day of Repentance, the litany is normally used.\nThe intercessions may begin with:\n{{r}}CL/L |{{/r}} Let us pray for the church and the world.\nEach petition is followed by a congregational response, sung or recited.",
						"alts": [],
						"selAlt": 0,
						"enabled": true,
						"optional": false,
						"salmeNr": "",
						"salmeTittel": ""
					},
					{
						"id": "i-mwrtxqzt-44",
						"type": "tekst",
						"heading": "either 1/3 (differing musical settings to the same text)",
						"instr": "@NOTAT We remember the dead and pray for those who are grieving.",
						"text": "{{r}}A |{{/r}} Lord, hear our prayer.\nBIBELREF | or 2\n{{r}}A |{{/r}} Hear our prayer. Hear our prayer. Your kingdom come, your will be done! Hear our prayer.\nBIBELREF | or 4\n{{r}}A |{{/r}} Lord, our God, hear us as we pray.\nAfter the final petition everyone sings: Amen.\nThe intercessions may conclude with the congregation remembering those who are dead, and those for whom funerals were held since the last occasion when the congregation gathered together.\n{{r}}CL/L |{{/r}} Let us stand and remember the members of our congregation for whom funerals have been held since we last gathered together.\nThe congregation stands. The names of the recently departed are read. A short silence is held.\n{{r}}CL/L |{{/r}} Teach us to count our days that we may gain a wise heart. Psalm 90:12\nor\n{{r}}CL/L |{{/r}} Jesus said: “I am the resurrection and the life. Those who believe in me, even though they die, will live.” John 11:25\nThe following prayer may be said thereafter, or another suitable prayer:\n{{r}}CL/L |{{/r}} Merciful God, comfort those in mourning and be close to them at this time.\nThe congregational response from the intercessions may then be repeated.\nPrayer stations may be integrated into the intercessions (section 18), or as a part of the communion when communal intercessions have taken place during the section for Intercessions. If a prayer is shared for those who have participated in the various intercession stations, this prayer is not combined with the Prayer of Thanksgiving for the eucharist after the meal.\n19 The offering\nThe congregation’s offering may take place at this point or during section 20, or alternatively during section 27.\nInstrumental or vocal music may be played during the offering. The collection may be taken up in the pews, or the congregation may offer gifts at the altar.\nThe offering may begin with:\n{{r}}L |{{/r}} Eternal God, the earth and all that fills it is yours. All that we have, belongs to you. We return to you a gift from your creation.\n{{r}}A/L |{{/r}} Receive us and our gifts in Jesus’ name. Amen.",
						"alts": [],
						"selAlt": 0,
						"enabled": true,
						"optional": false,
						"salmeNr": "",
						"salmeTittel": ""
					},
					{
						"id": "i-mwrtxqzt-45",
						"type": "tekst",
						"heading": "Holy Communion",
						"instr": "@NOTAT Communion hymn",
						"text": "20 The preparation of the meal\nThe congregation’s offering may be collected at this point, or during section 19, alternatively during section 27. The collection may occur before or during the hymn.\nBread and wine are then placed on the altar. Bread is placed on the plate, and wine is poured into the chalice.\nAfter the collection, the following words are said:\n{{r}}L |{{/r}} Blessed are you, God. The earth and all that fills it is yours. All that we have, belongs to you. We return to you a gift from your creation. Unite your church of all its peoples and languages. Like the grain has become one in bread and the grapes in wine, so bring us together as one and with the Lord Jesus Christ.\n{{r}}A/L |{{/r}} Receive us and our gifts in Jesus’ name. Amen.",
						"alts": [],
						"selAlt": 0,
						"enabled": true,
						"optional": false,
						"salmeNr": "",
						"salmeTittel": ""
					},
					{
						"id": "i-mwrtxqzt-46",
						"type": "tekst",
						"heading": "or",
						"instr": "",
						"text": "{{r}}L |{{/r}} Eternal God, the earth and all that fills it is yours. All that we have, belongs to you. We return to you a gift from your creation.\n{{r}}A/L |{{/r}} Receive us and our gifts in Jesus’ name. Amen.",
						"alts": [],
						"selAlt": 0,
						"enabled": true,
						"optional": false,
						"salmeNr": "",
						"salmeTittel": ""
					},
					{
						"id": "i-mwrtxqzt-47",
						"type": "tekst",
						"heading": "*21 Thanksgiving and prayer",
						"instr": "",
						"text": "",
						"alts": [],
						"selAlt": 0,
						"enabled": true,
						"optional": false,
						"salmeNr": "",
						"salmeTittel": ""
					},
					{
						"id": "i-mwrtxqzt-48",
						"type": "tekst",
						"heading": "Communion prayer A",
						"instr": "@NOTAT The greeting PREFACE DIALOGUE\n@NOTAT Introductory thanksgiving THE PREFACE\n@NOTAT Sundays in Trinity\n@NOTAT Holy, holy, holy SANCTUS",
						"text": "See Communion prayer B, Communion prayer C, Communion prayer D, Communion prayer D, Communion prayer E, Communion prayer F and Communion prayer G.\n{{r}}L |{{/r}} sings or says | The Lord be with you.\n{{r}}C |{{/r}} stands and sings | And also with you.\n{{r}}L |{{/r}} Lift up your hearts.\n{{r}}C |{{/r}} We lift our hearts to the Lord.\n{{r}}L |{{/r}} Let us give thanks to the Lord our God.\n{{r}}C |{{/r}} It is worthy and right to give thanks.\nThe liturgist faces the altar and sings or recites the preface.\nSee Prefaces for the Church Year.\n{{r}}L |{{/r}} It is truly worthy and right, our duty and our salvation always and everywhere to give you thanks, Father of holiness, Lord of heaven and earth, through our Lord Jesus Christ, whom you sent as a saviour to the world, so that we by his death should receive forgiveness of sins, and by his resurrection, we should gain eternal life. Through him the angels praise your glory, and heaven and earth sing forth your praise while we, with all the church, proclaim your glory in harmonious praise, singing:\nor\n{{r}}L |{{/r}} It is truly worthy and right, our duty and our salvation always and everywhere to give you thanks, Father of holiness, Lord of heaven and earth, through our Lord Jesus Christ. He is the living bread which descends from heaven and gives life to the world, so that whoever comes to him, will not hunger, and whoever believes in him, will not thirst. Through him the angels praise your glory, and heaven and earth sing forth your praise while we, with all the church, proclaim your glory in harmonious praise, singing:",
						"alts": [],
						"selAlt": 0,
						"enabled": true,
						"optional": false,
						"salmeNr": "",
						"salmeTittel": ""
					},
					{
						"id": "i-mwrtxqzt-49",
						"type": "tekst",
						"heading": "Series 1 & 2, and Series for festivals and Lent",
						"instr": "",
						"text": "{{r}}A |{{/r}} sing | Holy, holy, holy Lord.\nHeaven and earth are full of your glory.\nHosanna in the highest.\nBlessed is he who comes in the name of the Lord.\nHosanna in the highest.",
						"alts": [],
						"selAlt": 0,
						"enabled": true,
						"optional": false,
						"salmeNr": "",
						"salmeTittel": ""
					},
					{
						"id": "i-mwrtxqzt-50",
						"type": "tekst",
						"heading": "or",
						"instr": "@NOTAT Words of consecration VERBA",
						"text": "\nBIBELREF | Series 3\n{{r}}CL |{{/r}} and A sing\n{{r}}CL |{{/r}} Holy, holy, holy is our Lord God.\n{{r}}A |{{/r}} Holy, holy, holy is the Lord our God.\n{{r}}CL |{{/r}} You are Lord of heaven and earth.\n{{r}}A |{{/r}} Holy, holy, holy is the Lord our God.\n{{r}}CL |{{/r}} You are glorious, mighty and great.\n{{r}}A |{{/r}} Holy, holy, holy is the Lord our God.\n{{r}}CL |{{/r}} You have sent us Jesus Christ, your Son.\n{{r}}A |{{/r}} Holy, holy, holy is the Lord our God.\n{{r}}CL |{{/r}} Blessed is he who comes in the name of the Lord.\n{{r}}A |{{/r}} Holy, holy, holy is the Lord our God.\n{{r}}L/CL |{{/r}} We worship you, holy God, maker of heaven and earth. You so loved the world that you gave your only Son, Jesus Christ, so that he should save us from sin and death and gain a holy people.\n{{r}}L |{{/r}} We pray: Send down your spirit on us and these gifts, so that we may receive Jesus Christ in these gifts of bread and wine.\n{{r}}L |{{/r}} In the same night that he was betrayed, our Lord Jesus Christ took bread and gave you thanks; he broke it and gave it to his disciples, saying: Take, eat; this is my body which is given for you; do this in remembrance of me. In the same way, after supper he took the cup and gave you thanks; he gave it to them, saying: Drink this, all of you; this is my blood of the new covenant, which is shed for you and for many for the forgiveness of sins. Do this, as often as you drink it, in remembrance of me.\nDuring the Words of consecration, the priest first lifts the bread, then the wine.\nAfter the Words of consecration, the liturgist and the congregation may say:\n{{r}}L |{{/r}} Great is the mystery of faith.\n{{r}}A |{{/r}} Christ has died. Christ is risen. Christ will come again. Glory and praise to Christ for the love which is stronger than death.\n{{r}}L/CL |{{/r}} says | Gracious God, we celebrate this meal with joy and thanksgiving for the sacrifice of your son, believing in his victorious resurrection and ascension and in expectation of his return in glory. Fill us with your love, so that we may recognise Christ in those who hunger and thirst. Teach us to love one another as you have loved us, and grant that we one day may be gathered with you in your kingdom.\nThe communion liturgy continues with the Lord’s Prayer.",
						"alts": [],
						"selAlt": 0,
						"enabled": true,
						"optional": false,
						"salmeNr": "",
						"salmeTittel": ""
					},
					{
						"id": "i-mwrtxqzt-51",
						"type": "tekst",
						"heading": "Communion prayer B",
						"instr": "@NOTAT Greeting PREFACE DIALOGUE\n@NOTAT Introductory thanksgiving THE PREFACE\n@NOTAT Holy SANCTUS",
						"text": "{{r}}L |{{/r}} sings or says | The Lord be with you.\n{{r}}C |{{/r}} stands and sings | And also with you.\n{{r}}L |{{/r}} Lift up your hearts.\n{{r}}C |{{/r}} We lift our hearts to the Lord.\n{{r}}L |{{/r}} Let us give thanks to the Lord our God.\n{{r}}C |{{/r}} It is right and just to give thanks.\nThe liturgist faces the altar and sings or recites the preface, or the following words:\n{{r}}L |{{/r}} We thank you, God, through your Son Jesus Christ. He is the eternal word, and with this word you created everything. When the time came, you sent him to the world as our saviour and liberator. For this we praise you, together with all the angels in heaven and on the earth:",
						"alts": [],
						"selAlt": 0,
						"enabled": true,
						"optional": false,
						"salmeNr": "",
						"salmeTittel": ""
					},
					{
						"id": "i-mwrtxqzt-52",
						"type": "tekst",
						"heading": "Series 1 & 2, and Series for festivals and Lent",
						"instr": "",
						"text": "{{r}}A |{{/r}} sing| Holy, holy, holy Lord. Heaven and earth are full of your glory. Hosanna in the highest. Blessed is he who comes in the name of the Lord. Hosanna in the highest.",
						"alts": [],
						"selAlt": 0,
						"enabled": true,
						"optional": false,
						"salmeNr": "",
						"salmeTittel": ""
					},
					{
						"id": "i-mwrtxqzt-53",
						"type": "tekst",
						"heading": "or",
						"instr": "@NOTAT Words of consecration VERBA",
						"text": "\nBIBELREF | Series 3\n{{r}}CL |{{/r}} and A sing\n{{r}}CL |{{/r}} Holy, holy, holy is our Lord God.\n{{r}}A |{{/r}} Holy, holy, holy is the Lord our God.\n{{r}}CL |{{/r}} You are Lord of heaven and earth.\n{{r}}A |{{/r}} Holy, holy, holy is the Lord our God.\n{{r}}CL |{{/r}} You are glorious, mighty and great.\n{{r}}A |{{/r}} Holy, holy, holy is the Lord our God.\n{{r}}CL |{{/r}} You have sent us Jesus Christ, your Son.\n{{r}}A |{{/r}} Holy, holy, holy is the Lord our God.\n{{r}}CL |{{/r}} Blessed is he who comes in the name of the Lord.\n{{r}}A |{{/r}} Holy, holy, holy is the Lord our God.\n{{r}}L/CL |{{/r}} We praise you, God, for your servant Jesus Christ. He came from heaven, and by the Holy Spirit and the Virgin Mary, he became a human being of flesh and blood. His fulfilled your will when he stretched out his hands on the wood of the cross. Through this, he destroyed death, broke the chains of evil and revealed to us the resurrection of the body. Therefore, we remember his death and resurrection when we present the bread and wine to you.\n{{r}}L |{{/r}} We pray: Send down your Holy Spirit on these gifts, so that they for us become the bread of life and the cup of salvation.\n{{r}}L |{{/r}} In the same night that he was betrayed, our Lord Jesus Christ took bread and gave you thanks; he broke it and gave it to his disciples, saying: Take, eat; this is my body which is given for you; do this in remembrance of me. In the same way, after supper he took the cup and gave you thanks; he gave it to them, saying: Drink this, all of you; this is my blood of the new covenant, which is shed for you and for many for the forgiveness of sins. Do this, as often as you drink it, in remembrance of me.\nDuring the Words of consecration, the priest first lifts the bread, then the wine.\nAfter the Words of consecration, the liturgist and the congregation may say:\n{{r}}L |{{/r}} Great is the mystery of faith.\n{{r}}A |{{/r}} Christ has died. Christ is risen. Christ will come again. Glory and praise to Christ for the love which is stronger than death.\n{{r}}L/CL |{{/r}} Grant that all who take part in this bread and wine be united as one. Fill us with your Holy Spirit and grant us a foundation of truth, so that we may praise you and live to your glory.\nThe communion liturgy continues with the Lord’s Prayer.",
						"alts": [],
						"selAlt": 0,
						"enabled": true,
						"optional": false,
						"salmeNr": "",
						"salmeTittel": ""
					},
					{
						"id": "i-mwrtxqzu-54",
						"type": "tekst",
						"heading": "Communion prayer C",
						"instr": "@NOTAT Greeting PREFACE DIALOGUE\n@NOTAT Introductory thanksgiving THE PREFACE\n@NOTAT Holy SANCTUS",
						"text": "{{r}}L |{{/r}} sings or says | The Lord be with you.\n{{r}}C |{{/r}} stands and sings | And also with you.\n{{r}}L |{{/r}} Lift up your hearts.\n{{r}}C |{{/r}} We lift our hearts to the Lord.\n{{r}}L |{{/r}} Let us give thanks to the Lord our God.\n{{r}}C |{{/r}} It is right and just to give thanks.\nThe liturgist faces the altar and sings or recites the preface, or the following words:\n{{r}}L |{{/r}} The depth of your riches, wisdom and knowledge is boundless, O God! The heavens tell of your glory and the earth witness to the work of your hands. Together with the faithful through the ages we bless your holy name:",
						"alts": [],
						"selAlt": 0,
						"enabled": true,
						"optional": false,
						"salmeNr": "",
						"salmeTittel": ""
					},
					{
						"id": "i-mwrtxqzu-55",
						"type": "tekst",
						"heading": "Series 1 & 2, and Series for festivals and Lent",
						"instr": "",
						"text": "{{r}}A |{{/r}} sing| Holy, holy, holy Lord.\nHeaven and earth are full of your glory.\nHosanna in the highest.\nBlessed is he who comes in the name of the Lord.\nHosanna in the highest.",
						"alts": [],
						"selAlt": 0,
						"enabled": true,
						"optional": false,
						"salmeNr": "",
						"salmeTittel": ""
					},
					{
						"id": "i-mwrtxqzu-56",
						"type": "tekst",
						"heading": "or",
						"instr": "@NOTAT Words of consecration VERBA",
						"text": "\nBIBELREF | Series 3\n{{r}}CL |{{/r}} and A sing\n{{r}}CL |{{/r}} Holy, holy, holy is our Lord God.\n{{r}}A |{{/r}} Holy, holy, holy is the Lord our God.\n{{r}}CL |{{/r}} You are Lord of heaven and earth.\n{{r}}A |{{/r}} Holy, holy, holy is the Lord our God.\n{{r}}CL |{{/r}} You are glorious, mighty and great.\n{{r}}A |{{/r}} Holy, holy, holy is the Lord our God.\n{{r}}CL |{{/r}} You have sent us Jesus Christ, your Son.\n{{r}}A |{{/r}} Holy, holy, holy is the Lord our God.\n{{r}}CL |{{/r}} Blessed is he who comes in the name of the Lord.\n{{r}}A |{{/r}} Holy, holy, holy is the Lord our God.\n{{r}}L |{{/r}} Holy and merciful God, you did not abandon your people when they sinned,\nbut gave your promise to Abraham to bless all peoples.\nAlmighty and faithful God, you freed your people from captivity,\nand renewed them with your promises through the prophets.\nWhen the time came, you sent your Son, born of Mary,\nto set us free and grant us the right to be your children.\nBy his death on the cross, you reconciled all with yourself and made peace, and through His resurrection, conquered death. Send your Spirit over us and your gifts. Unite us in faith in your grace, so that we may receive the body and blood of Christ in reconciliation and peace, and proclaim his death until he comes again.\n{{r}}L |{{/r}} In the same night that he was betrayed, our Lord Jesus Christ took bread and gave you thanks; he broke it and gave it to his disciples, saying: Take, eat; this is my body which is given for you; do this in remembrance of me. In the same way, after supper he took the cup and gave you thanks; he gave it to them, saying: Drink this, all of you; this is my blood of the new covenant, which is shed for you and for many for the forgiveness of sins. Do this, as often as you drink it, in remembrance of me.\nDuring the Words of consecration, the priest first lifts the bread, then the wine.\nAfter the Words of consecration, the liturgist and the congregation may say:\n{{r}}L |{{/r}} Great is the mystery of faith.\n{{r}}A |{{/r}} Christ has died. Christ is risen. Christ will come again. Glory and praise to Christ for the love which is stronger than death.\n{{r}}L/CL |{{/r}} Eternal God, renew us with your Spirit. Together with all that is made, we wait with longing to be freed from mortality and to take part in the freedom which your children will share in glory. All that is, visible and invisible is in you and with you and through you. To you be the glory for all eternity!\nThe communion liturgy continues with the Lord’s Prayer.",
						"alts": [],
						"selAlt": 0,
						"enabled": true,
						"optional": false,
						"salmeNr": "",
						"salmeTittel": ""
					},
					{
						"id": "i-mwrtxqzu-57",
						"type": "tekst",
						"heading": "Communion prayer D",
						"instr": "@NOTAT Greeting PREFACE DIALOGUE\n@NOTAT Introductory thanksgiving THE PREFACE\n@NOTAT Holy SANCTUS",
						"text": "{{r}}L |{{/r}} sings or says | The Lord be with you.\n{{r}}C |{{/r}} stands and sings | And also with you.\n{{r}}L |{{/r}} Lift up your hearts.\n{{r}}C |{{/r}} We lift our hearts to the Lord.\n{{r}}L |{{/r}} Let us give thanks to the Lord our God.\n{{r}}C |{{/r}} It is right and just to give thanks.\nThe liturgist faces the altar and sings or recites the preface, or the following words:\n{{r}}L |{{/r}} We praise you, eternal God, you who have made the earth and all that is in it. In you we live, move and have our being. Together with your congregation in heaven and on the earth, we praise your holy name:",
						"alts": [],
						"selAlt": 0,
						"enabled": true,
						"optional": false,
						"salmeNr": "",
						"salmeTittel": ""
					},
					{
						"id": "i-mwrtxqzu-58",
						"type": "tekst",
						"heading": "Series 1 & 2, and Series for festivals and Lent",
						"instr": "",
						"text": "{{r}}A |{{/r}} sing| Holy, holy, holy Lord.\nHeaven and earth are full of your glory.\nHosanna in the highest.\nBlessed is he who comes in the name of the Lord.\nHosanna in the highest.",
						"alts": [],
						"selAlt": 0,
						"enabled": true,
						"optional": false,
						"salmeNr": "",
						"salmeTittel": ""
					},
					{
						"id": "i-mwrtxqzu-59",
						"type": "tekst",
						"heading": "or",
						"instr": "@NOTAT Words of consecration VERBA",
						"text": "\nBIBELREF | Series 3\n{{r}}CL |{{/r}} and A sing\n{{r}}CL |{{/r}} Holy, holy, holy is our Lord God.\n{{r}}A |{{/r}} Holy, holy, holy is the Lord our God.\n{{r}}CL |{{/r}} You are Lord of heaven and earth.\n{{r}}A |{{/r}} Holy, holy, holy is the Lord our God.\n{{r}}CL |{{/r}} You are glorious, mighty and great.\n{{r}}A |{{/r}} Holy, holy, holy is the Lord our God.\n{{r}}CL |{{/r}} You have sent us Jesus Christ, your Son.\n{{r}}A |{{/r}} Holy, holy, holy is the Lord our God.\n{{r}}CL |{{/r}} Blessed is he who comes in the name of the Lord.\n{{r}}A |{{/r}} Holy, holy, holy is the Lord our God.\n{{r}}L/CL |{{/r}} We thank you, source of all goodness. You sent your Son. He was crucified and rose from the dead. He unlocked the scriptures and revealed himself to his friends when he broke bread and gave it to them.\n{{r}}L |{{/r}} Now we pray: May your Holy Spirit come down upon this bread and wine, so that our eyes may be opened, and we might know him again as our crucified and risen saviour.\n{{r}}L |{{/r}} In the same night that he was betrayed, our Lord Jesus Christ took bread and gave you thanks; he broke it and gave it to his disciples, saying: Take, eat; this is my body which is given for you; do this in remembrance of me. In the same way, after supper he took the cup and gave you thanks; he gave it to them, saying: Drink this, all of you; this is my blood of the new covenant, which is shed for you and for many for the forgiveness of sins. Do this, as often as you drink it, in remembrance of me.\nDuring the Words of consecration, the priest first lifts the bread, then the wine.\nAfter the Words of consecration, the liturgist and the congregation may say:\n{{r}}L |{{/r}} Great is the mystery of faith.\n{{r}}A |{{/r}} Christ has died. Christ is risen. Christ will come again. Glory and praise to Christ for the love which is stronger than death.\n{{r}}L/CL |{{/r}} says | Holy God, fill us with your Holy Spirit. Give us burning hearts, so that we in wonder and joy may be true to your word and show mercy to those who suffer. Be with us, also in our doubts and sorrows. Walk with us, until loss and grief have given way to your eternal gladness.\nThe communion liturgy continues with the Lord’s Prayer.",
						"alts": [],
						"selAlt": 0,
						"enabled": true,
						"optional": false,
						"salmeNr": "",
						"salmeTittel": ""
					},
					{
						"id": "i-mwrtxqzu-60",
						"type": "tekst",
						"heading": "Communion prayer E",
						"instr": "@NOTAT Greeting PREFACE DIALOGUE\n@NOTAT Introductory thanksgiving THE PREFACE\n@NOTAT Holy SANCTUS",
						"text": "{{r}}L |{{/r}} sings or says | The Lord be with you.\n{{r}}C |{{/r}} stands and sings | And also with you.\n{{r}}L |{{/r}} Lift up your hearts.\n{{r}}C |{{/r}} We lift our hearts to the Lord.\n{{r}}L |{{/r}} Let us give thanks to the Lord our God.\n{{r}}C |{{/r}} It is worthy and right to give thanks.\nThe liturgist faces the altar and sings or recites the preface, or the following words:\n{{r}}L |{{/r}} We give you thanks, gracious God, you who hold the heaven and the earth in your hands. Together with the angels and your congregation in heaven and on earth, we praise your holy name:",
						"alts": [],
						"selAlt": 0,
						"enabled": true,
						"optional": false,
						"salmeNr": "",
						"salmeTittel": ""
					},
					{
						"id": "i-mwrtxqzu-61",
						"type": "tekst",
						"heading": "Series 1 & 2, and Series for festivals and Lent",
						"instr": "",
						"text": "{{r}}A |{{/r}} sing | Holy, holy, holy Lord.\nHeaven and earth are full of your glory.\nHosanna in the highest.\nBlessed is he who comes in the name of the Lord.\nHosanna in the highest.",
						"alts": [],
						"selAlt": 0,
						"enabled": true,
						"optional": false,
						"salmeNr": "",
						"salmeTittel": ""
					},
					{
						"id": "i-mwrtxqzu-62",
						"type": "tekst",
						"heading": "or",
						"instr": "@NOTAT Words of consecration VERBA",
						"text": "\nBIBELREF | Series 3\n{{r}}CL |{{/r}} and A sing\n{{r}}CL |{{/r}} Holy, holy, holy is our Lord God.\n{{r}}A |{{/r}} Holy, holy, holy is the Lord our God.\n{{r}}CL |{{/r}} You are Lord of heaven and earth.\n{{r}}A |{{/r}} Holy, holy, holy is the Lord our God.\n{{r}}CL |{{/r}} You are glorious, mighty and great.\n{{r}}A |{{/r}} Holy, holy, holy is the Lord our God.\n{{r}}CL |{{/r}} You have sent us Jesus Christ, your Son.\n{{r}}A |{{/r}} Holy, holy, holy is the Lord our God.\n{{r}}CL |{{/r}} Blessed is he who comes in the name of the Lord.\n{{r}}A |{{/r}} Holy, holy, holy is the Lord our God.\n{{r}}L/CL |{{/r}} Holy God, we thank you for Jesus Christ, the saviour of the world. He died and rose again, so that we may have eternal life. We thank you for the gift of baptism, where we are born anew, and for the Communion, where you gather us together as your great family.\n{{r}}L |{{/r}} Now we pray: May your Holy Spirit come down upon this bread and wine. Make us one with each other and with Jesus Christ.\n{{r}}L |{{/r}} In the same night that he was betrayed, our Lord Jesus Christ took bread and gave you thanks; he broke it and gave it to his disciples, saying: Take, eat; this is my body which is given for you; do this in remembrance of me. In the same way, after supper he took the cup and gave you thanks; he gave it to them, saying: Drink this, all of you; this is my blood of the new covenant, which is shed for you and for many for the forgiveness of sins. Do this, as often as you drink it, in remembrance of me.\nDuring the Words of consecration, the priest first lifts the bread, then the wine.\nAfter the Words of consecration, the liturgist and the congregation may say:\n{{r}}L |{{/r}} Great is the mystery of faith.\n{{r}}A |{{/r}} Christ has died. Christ is risen. Christ will come again. Glory and praise to Christ for the love which is stronger than death.\n{{r}}L/CL |{{/r}} sings or says | God, fill us with your Spirit. Embrace us all, just as a loving mother gathers her children around her. Let the meek and lowly be uplifted, and the hungry filled with good things.\nThe liturgist and/or one or more children sing(s) or say(s):\nLet us together with all of your children say the prayer which your Son has taught us:\nThe communion liturgy continues with the Lord’s Prayer.",
						"alts": [],
						"selAlt": 0,
						"enabled": true,
						"optional": false,
						"salmeNr": "",
						"salmeTittel": ""
					},
					{
						"id": "i-mwrtxqzu-63",
						"type": "tekst",
						"heading": "Communion prayer F",
						"instr": "@NOTAT Greeting PREFACE DIALOGUE\n@NOTAT Introductory thanksgiving THE PREFACE\n@NOTAT Holy SANCTUS",
						"text": "This short communion prayer may be used for special occasions, for instance when there are many baptisms in the service.\n\n{{r}}L |{{/r}} sings or says | The Lord be with you.\n{{r}}C |{{/r}} stands and sings | And also with you.\n{{r}}L |{{/r}} Lift up your hearts.\n{{r}}C |{{/r}} We lift our hearts to the Lord.\n{{r}}L |{{/r}} Let us give thanks to the Lord our God.\n{{r}}C |{{/r}} It is right and just to give thanks.\nThe liturgist faces the altar and sings or recites the preface, or the following words:\n{{r}}L |{{/r}} Good God, you have created us and called us by our names. You open your hand and feed all beings that live in grace. Together with your congregation in heaven and on earth, we praise your holy name:",
						"alts": [],
						"selAlt": 0,
						"enabled": true,
						"optional": false,
						"salmeNr": "",
						"salmeTittel": ""
					},
					{
						"id": "i-mwrtxqzu-64",
						"type": "tekst",
						"heading": "Series 1 & 2, and Series for festivals and Lent",
						"instr": "",
						"text": "{{r}}A |{{/r}} sing | Holy, holy, holy Lord.\nHeaven and earth are full of your glory.\nHosanna in the highest.\nBlessed is he who comes in the name of the Lord.\nHosanna in the highest.",
						"alts": [],
						"selAlt": 0,
						"enabled": true,
						"optional": false,
						"salmeNr": "",
						"salmeTittel": ""
					},
					{
						"id": "i-mwrtxqzu-65",
						"type": "tekst",
						"heading": "or",
						"instr": "@NOTAT Words of consecration VERBA",
						"text": "\nBIBELREF | Series 3\n{{r}}CL |{{/r}} and A sing\n{{r}}CL |{{/r}} Holy, holy, holy is our Lord God.\n{{r}}A |{{/r}} Holy, holy, holy is the Lord our God.\n{{r}}CL |{{/r}} You are Lord of heaven and earth.\n{{r}}A |{{/r}} Holy, holy, holy is the Lord our God.\n{{r}}CL |{{/r}} You are glorious, mighty and great.\n{{r}}A |{{/r}} Holy, holy, holy is the Lord our God.\n{{r}}CL |{{/r}} You have sent us Jesus Christ, your Son.\n{{r}}A |{{/r}} Holy, holy, holy is the Lord our God.\n{{r}}CL |{{/r}} Blessed is he who comes in the name of the Lord.\n{{r}}A |{{/r}} Holy, holy, holy is the Lord our God.\n{{r}}L/CL |{{/r}} We thank you for Jesus Christ, our savour. He is the living bread that comes from heaven and gives life to the world.\n{{r}}L |{{/r}} We pray: Send down your Holy Spirit on us and these gifts, so that we may receive Jesus Christ in the bread and wine.\n{{r}}L |{{/r}} In the same night that he was betrayed, our Lord Jesus Christ took bread and gave you thanks; he broke it and gave it to his disciples, saying: Take, eat; this is my body which is given for you; do this in remembrance of me. In the same way, after supper he took the cup and gave you thanks; he gave it to them, saying: Drink this, all of you; this is my blood of the new covenant, which is shed for you and for many for the forgiveness of sins. Do this, as often as you drink it, in remembrance of me.\nAfter the Words of consecration, the liturgist and the congregation may say:\n{{r}}L |{{/r}} Great is the mystery of faith.\n{{r}}A |{{/r}} Christ has died. Christ is risen. Christ will come again. Glory and praise to Christ for the love which is stronger than death.\n{{r}}L/CL |{{/r}} sings or says | Let us together with all your children say the prayer which your Son has taught us:\nThe communion liturgy continues with the Lord’s Prayer.",
						"alts": [],
						"selAlt": 0,
						"enabled": true,
						"optional": false,
						"salmeNr": "",
						"salmeTittel": ""
					},
					{
						"id": "i-mwrtxqzu-66",
						"type": "tekst",
						"heading": "Communion prayer G",
						"instr": "@NOTAT Greeting PREFACE DIALOGUE\n@NOTAT Introductory thanksgiving THE PREFACE\n@NOTAT Holy SANCTUS",
						"text": "{{r}}L |{{/r}} sings or says | The Lord be with you.\n{{r}}C |{{/r}} stands and sings | And also with you.\n{{r}}L |{{/r}} Lift up your hearts.\n{{r}}C |{{/r}} We lift our hearts to the Lord.\n{{r}}L |{{/r}} Let us give thanks to the Lord our God.\n{{r}}C |{{/r}} It is right and just to give thanks.\nThe liturgist faces the altar and sings or recites the preface, or the following words:\n{{r}}L |{{/r}} Eternal, almighty God, you hold heaven and earth in your hands, you call us by our names so that we may belong to you and be your people earth. Together with your followers throughout time and with your heavenly hosts, we praise your holy name:",
						"alts": [],
						"selAlt": 0,
						"enabled": true,
						"optional": false,
						"salmeNr": "",
						"salmeTittel": ""
					},
					{
						"id": "i-mwrtxqzu-67",
						"type": "tekst",
						"heading": "Series 1 & 2, and Series for festivals and Lent",
						"instr": "",
						"text": "{{r}}A |{{/r}} sing | Holy, holy, holy Lord.\nHeaven and earth are full of your glory.\nHosanna in the highest.\nBlessed is he who comes in the name of the Lord.\nHosanna in the highest.",
						"alts": [],
						"selAlt": 0,
						"enabled": true,
						"optional": false,
						"salmeNr": "",
						"salmeTittel": ""
					},
					{
						"id": "i-mwrtxqzu-68",
						"type": "tekst",
						"heading": "or",
						"instr": "@NOTAT Words of consecration VERBA\n@NOTAT All communion prayers continue thus:\n@NOTAT The Lord’s Prayer",
						"text": "\nBIBELREF | Series 3\n{{r}}CL |{{/r}} and A sing\n{{r}}CL |{{/r}} Holy, holy, holy is our Lord God.\n{{r}}A |{{/r}} Holy, holy, holy is the Lord our God.\n{{r}}CL |{{/r}} You are Lord of heaven and earth.\n{{r}}A |{{/r}} Holy, holy, holy is the Lord our God.\n{{r}}CL |{{/r}} You are glorious, mighty and great.\n{{r}}A |{{/r}} Holy, holy, holy is the Lord our God.\n{{r}}CL |{{/r}} You have sent us Jesus Christ, your Son.\n{{r}}A |{{/r}} Holy, holy, holy is the Lord our God.\n{{r}}CL |{{/r}} Blessed is he who comes in the name of the Lord.\n{{r}}A |{{/r}} Holy, holy, holy is the Lord our God.\n{{r}}L/CL |{{/r}} Holy God, your mercy is without ending, your reign is eternal. You have filled your creation with light and life; heaven and earth are full of your glory. Through Abraham you promised to bless all peoples. You scorned Israel, your chosen people. Through the prophets you renewed your vow. And when the time came, you sent your Son, he whom in word and deed preached of your Kingdom, and obeyed your will until death.\n{{r}}L |{{/r}} We pray: Send down your Holy Spirit on these gifts, so that we may receive Jesus Christ in the bread and wine.\n{{r}}L |{{/r}} In the same night that he was betrayed, our Lord Jesus Christ took bread and gave you thanks; he broke it and gave it to his disciples, saying: Take, eat; this is my body which is given for you; do this in remembrance of me. In the same way, after supper he took the cup and gave you thanks; he gave it to them, saying: Drink this, all of you; this is my blood of the new covenant, which is shed for you and for many for the forgiveness of sins. Do this, as often as you drink it, in remembrance of me.\n{{r}}L/CL |{{/r}} Therefore, as often as we eat this bread and drink from this cup, we are witnesses of the Lord’s death, until he comes.\nDuring the Words of consecration, the priest first lifts the bread, then the wine.\nAfter the Words of consecration, the liturgist and the congregation may say:\n{{r}}L |{{/r}} Great is the mystery of faith.\n{{r}}A |{{/r}} Christ has died. Christ is risen. Christ will come again. Glory and praise to Christ for the love which is stronger than death.\n{{r}}L/CL |{{/r}} Therefore, merciful Father, we will with this bread and this cup remember that the Lord gave his life for us. And trusting in his resurrection, we wait for him to come again in power and glory, and will hold his great feast together with his people.\n{{r}}A |{{/r}} Amen, yes, come, Lord Jesus.\n{{r}}L |{{/r}} We pray, almighty God, send us your Holy Spirit. Let us feel the power of the resurrection of Christ, so that we who receive his body and blood, may live in praise and honour for your glory, and share in the heritage that your holy children receive in light.\nThe communion liturgy continues with the Lord’s Prayer.\nSaid or sung.\n{{r}}A |{{/r}} Our Father in heaven,\nhallowed be your name,\nyour kingdom come,\nyour will be done,\non earth as in heaven.\nGive us today our daily bread.",
						"alts": [],
						"selAlt": 0,
						"enabled": true,
						"optional": false,
						"salmeNr": "",
						"salmeTittel": ""
					},
					{
						"id": "i-mwrtxqzu-69",
						"type": "tekst",
						"heading": "Forgive us our sins",
						"instr": "",
						"text": "as we forgive those who sin against us.",
						"alts": [],
						"selAlt": 0,
						"enabled": true,
						"optional": false,
						"salmeNr": "",
						"salmeTittel": ""
					},
					{
						"id": "i-mwrtxqzu-70",
						"type": "tekst",
						"heading": "Lead us not into temptation",
						"instr": "",
						"text": "but deliver us from evil.\nFor the kingdom, the power,\nand the glory are yours\nnow and for ever.\nAmen.\nOther recognised translations of the Lord ’s Prayer may be used instead.",
						"alts": [],
						"selAlt": 0,
						"enabled": true,
						"optional": false,
						"salmeNr": "",
						"salmeTittel": ""
					},
					{
						"id": "i-mwrtxqzu-71",
						"type": "tekst",
						"heading": "* 22 The meal",
						"instr": "@NOTAT The peace PAX\n@NOTAT Breaking of the bread\n@NOTAT Lamb of God AGNUS DEI",
						"text": "The congregation remains standing until the first congregants proceed to receive communion.\n{{r}}L |{{/r}} The peace of God be with you.\n{{r}}C |{{/r}} The peace of God be with you.\nHere may follow:\n{{r}}L/CL |{{/r}} Let us offer one another a sign of peace.\nThe congregation greet each other with a handshake and say “God’s peace” or “The peace of Christ” or similar words.\nHere may follow:\nWhen the bread is broken, the priest may say:\n{{r}}L |{{/r}} We break this bread to share in the body of Christ. In this one bread, we are joined together in one body.",
						"alts": [],
						"selAlt": 0,
						"enabled": true,
						"optional": false,
						"salmeNr": "",
						"salmeTittel": ""
					},
					{
						"id": "i-mwrtxqzu-72",
						"type": "tekst",
						"heading": "Series 1 & 2, and Series for festivals and Lent",
						"instr": "@NOTAT The distribution\n@NOTAT The thanksgiving prayer",
						"text": "{{r}}A |{{/r}} sing | Lamb of God, you take away the sin of the world, have mercy on us.\nLamb of God, you take away the sin of the world, have mercy on us.\nLamb of God, you take away the sin of the world, grant us peace.\nBIBELREF | Series 3\n{{r}}CL |{{/r}} and A sing\n{{r}}CL |{{/r}} Amen, come, Lord Jesus.\n{{r}}C |{{/r}} Amen, come, Lord Jesus.\n{{r}}CL |{{/r}} You are the Lamb that takes away our sins.\n{{r}}C |{{/r}} Amen, come, Lord Jesus.\n{{r}}CL |{{/r}} You are the Lamb that grants us peace.\n{{r}}C |{{/r}} Amen, come, Lord Jesus.\n{{r}}CL |{{/r}} You are the bread that gives us your life.\n{{r}}C |{{/r}} Amen, come, Lord Jesus.\n{{r}}L |{{/r}} says | Come forward, everything is ready.\nThe invitation may be made before the Agnus Dei is sung.\nDuring the distribution hymns or anthems may be sung, or appropriate instrumental music may be performed.\nThe words of distribution words:\nThe body of Christ, given for you.\nThe blood of Christ, shed for you.\nAlternatively, these words may be used:\nThis is the body of Christ.\nThis is the blood of Christ.\nThose who come forward and indicate that they do not wish to receive Communion may be blessed by the priest or co-liturgist distributing the bread, by the laying on of hands or the sign of the cross.\nThe following or similar words may be used:\nThe Lord bless you and keep you and lead you to eternal life.\nWhen the elements are distributed in kneeling groups around the alter, the blessing of peace may be given either after the last group, or after each kneeling group.\nAfter the distribution:\n{{r}}L |{{/r}} says | The crucified and risen Jesus Christ has given us his holy body and blood which he gave as atonement for all our sins.\n{{r}}A |{{/r}} (or L) | May he strengthen us and uphold us in true faith to eternal life.\n{{r}}L |{{/r}} Peace be with you.\n23 The conclusion of the meal\nThe altar is cleared. The chalice(s) and plate(s) are covered with a chalice cloth.\nHere, the liturgist/co-liturgist may say or sing:\n{{r}}L/CL |{{/r}} Let us give thanks and pray.\n{{r}}L/CL |{{/r}} We thank you, heavenly Father, for your blessed gifts.\nWe pray that, with these gifts, you will preserve our faith in you, unite us in your love and confirm us in the hope of eternal life, in the name of Jesus Christ.",
						"alts": [],
						"selAlt": 0,
						"enabled": true,
						"optional": false,
						"salmeNr": "",
						"salmeTittel": ""
					},
					{
						"id": "i-mwrtxqzu-73",
						"type": "tekst",
						"heading": "or",
						"instr": "",
						"text": "{{r}}L/CL |{{/r}} We thank you, God of wisdom, for the mystery of the Communion. The bread we have broken, is one bread. Your Son has given his life for one world and one people.\n{{r}}A |{{/r}} or L/CL | We pray: help us to hear the cry you have heard, to see the need you have seen, and to love our neighbours as ourselves.",
						"alts": [],
						"selAlt": 0,
						"enabled": true,
						"optional": false,
						"salmeNr": "",
						"salmeTittel": ""
					},
					{
						"id": "i-mwrtxqzu-74",
						"type": "tekst",
						"heading": "or",
						"instr": "",
						"text": "{{r}}L/CL |{{/r}} We thank you, gracious God, who through this bread and wine have allowed us to participate in Jesus Christ’s victorious death and resurrection.\n{{r}}A |{{/r}} or L/CL | Strengthen us with your Holy Spirit to witness and serve in the world.",
						"alts": [],
						"selAlt": 0,
						"enabled": true,
						"optional": false,
						"salmeNr": "",
						"salmeTittel": ""
					},
					{
						"id": "i-mwrtxqzu-75",
						"type": "tekst",
						"heading": "or",
						"instr": "",
						"text": "{{r}}L/CL |{{/r}} Faithful God, you who in baptism has made us your children, and made us heirs of your kingdom. We thank you for this meal, in which you have given us forgiveness of sins and renewed our faith in your promises. We pray:\n{{r}}A |{{/r}} or L/CL | Strengthen us with your Holy Sprit to witness and serve in the world.",
						"alts": [],
						"selAlt": 0,
						"enabled": true,
						"optional": false,
						"salmeNr": "",
						"salmeTittel": ""
					},
					{
						"id": "i-mwrtxqzu-76",
						"type": "tekst",
						"heading": "The Dismissal",
						"instr": "",
						"text": "",
						"alts": [],
						"selAlt": 0,
						"enabled": true,
						"optional": false,
						"salmeNr": "",
						"salmeTittel": ""
					},
					{
						"id": "i-mwrtxqzu-77",
						"type": "tekst",
						"heading": "*24 Hymn",
						"instr": "",
						"text": "This hymn may be moved to Postlude/Recessional, section 27.\n",
						"alts": [],
						"selAlt": 0,
						"enabled": true,
						"optional": false,
						"salmeNr": "",
						"salmeTittel": ""
					},
					{
						"id": "i-mwrtxqzu-78",
						"type": "tekst",
						"heading": "*25 The blessing",
						"instr": "@NOTAT Praise BENEDICAMUS",
						"text": "This blessing may also be used in services other than the High Mass.\nThe blessing may be sead or sung.\nThe blessing may be received by each individual by making the sign of the cross.\nThe introduction to the blessing may be formed thus:\n{{r}}L/ML |{{/r}} sings or says | Let us praise the Lord.\n{{r}}A |{{/r}} God be praised. Alleluia. Alleluia. Alleluia.",
						"alts": [],
						"selAlt": 0,
						"enabled": true,
						"optional": false,
						"salmeNr": "",
						"salmeTittel": ""
					},
					{
						"id": "i-mwrtxqzu-79",
						"type": "tekst",
						"heading": "or",
						"instr": "@NOTAT Salutation SALUTATIO",
						"text": "{{r}}L |{{/r}} sings or says | The Lord be with you.\n{{r}}C |{{/r}} And also with you.",
						"alts": [],
						"selAlt": 0,
						"enabled": true,
						"optional": false,
						"salmeNr": "",
						"salmeTittel": ""
					},
					{
						"id": "i-mwrtxqzu-80",
						"type": "tekst",
						"heading": "or",
						"instr": "@NOTAT A bell is rung nine times, in sets of three.",
						"text": "{{r}}L |{{/r}} says | Receive the blessing.\n{{r}}L |{{/r}} The Lord bless you and keep you.\nThe Lord make his face shine upon you and be gracious to you.\nThe Lord lift up his countenance upon you and give you peace. \nThe congregation may sing or say:\n{{r}}C |{{/r}} Amen. Amen. Amen.",
						"alts": [],
						"selAlt": 0,
						"enabled": true,
						"optional": false,
						"salmeNr": "",
						"salmeTittel": ""
					},
					{
						"id": "i-mwrtxqzu-81",
						"type": "tekst",
						"heading": "* 26 The dismissal",
						"instr": "",
						"text": "If the congregation remains seated during the following postlude, the words of dismissal may be said after the postlude.\nHere may follow:\n{{r}}L/CL |{{/r}} Let us go in peace,\n{{r}}A |{{/r}} in the name of Christ.",
						"alts": [],
						"selAlt": 0,
						"enabled": true,
						"optional": false,
						"salmeNr": "",
						"salmeTittel": ""
					},
					{
						"id": "i-mwrtxqzu-82",
						"type": "tekst",
						"heading": "or",
						"instr": "",
						"text": "{{r}}L/CL |{{/r}} Go in peace. Serve the Lord with gladness.\n27 Postlude/Recessional\nWhen there is a recessional, the congregation may follow the procession. A congregational hymn may replace the postlude.\nThe church may remain open for a while after the service, allowing for silent prayer and reflection.\nThe diaconal aspects of the dismissal may be followed up through gatherings, home visits, prayers and other parish responsibilities.\nOrdning for hovedgudstjeneste 2020 - engelsk oversettelse The order of the Principal Service 2020: English translation (Updated 2021)\n{{r}}PAGE |{{/r}} \\* MERGEFORMAT31",
						"alts": [],
						"selAlt": 0,
						"enabled": true,
						"optional": false,
						"salmeNr": "",
						"salmeTittel": ""
					}
				]
			}
		],
		"visInstr": true,
